<title>GERMANY: Tietmeyer - Italy must be treated fairly over EMU.</title>
<headline>Tietmeyer - Italy must be treated fairly over EMU.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1997-02-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank President Hans Tietmeyer said on Saturday that Italy must be treated equally in its bid to gain entry into the planned European currency slated to start in January 1999.</p>
<p>Tietmeyer said financial leaders at the Group of Seven (G7) meeting on Saturday in Berlin did not talk about the entry of specific countries into currency union.</p>
<p>Tietmeyer said he did not understand the irritation regarding Italy's bid to enter currency union and noted that no discussion has taken place among central bankers to give preference to or discriminate against certain countries.</p>
<p>--Berlin Newsroom, +49 30 2039810</p>
</text>
